WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've had people like
Jeff Daniels and Keri Russell,

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.902 size:81% position:41%
who are actors who are
on Broadway right now,

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm always fascinated
by the distractions

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
that might happen
with a Broadway audience

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:08.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
because obviously people are
very excited to be there.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:10.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, but it is live,
and all it takes is one person

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
doing something that could
maybe, as an actor,

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of pull you
out of the moment.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is the worst
you've had to deal with?

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's interesting,
because on your show,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.154
if there was a distraction here,
you would just cut the tape.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-And no one would really know.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when you're doing
live theater, it happens.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's there.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:30.296
Well, what's interesting is that
when an actor is on stage,

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:34.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's normal to feel an audienc
looking from right to left

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:35.668 size:81% position:41% line:92%
at the actor speaking.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this movement -- horizontal
movement is natural.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:42.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
What isn't natural is
when someone is doing this

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:47.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
And once when I was playing LB
in a play here

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:47.947 size:78% position:39% line:92%
called "All the Way,"

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:52.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was a kid about
16 years old, very front row

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:56.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
right in the front
and right in the middle.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.292 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And he was doing this.

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.294 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.529 line:92%
And it was catching my eye

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:04.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I walked over to see
what he was doing.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I kind of looked down
from the stage.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.302 line:92%
And I saw he had his phone

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no.
-In his lap.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was like --
[ Audience aws ]

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
Aw, aw.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:17.277
Very sympathetic audience.
-Yeah, very sympathetic.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:20.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Aw.
And he was doing this.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:25.919 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got upset.
-Sure.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.824
-I did.
I started to get a little angry.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.592 line:92%
Primarily because his parent

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
were two seats away
and saying nothing.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought,
"Well, that's kind of rude."

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:43.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I realized that my next
speech was a fiery one

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:48.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
filled with anger
and vitriol and spittle.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.709 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:54.714
So I adjusted the blocking
to come right downstage.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Screaming ]

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.118 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:01.020 line:92%
And my spit is flying at him

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And I swear to God.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:06.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
The kid's like --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:07.560 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Oh, no."

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is --
-Yeah.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:12.232 line:92%
I spat on an audience member

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, that --
what a gift, though,

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.336
that you're playing someone like
LBJ, who's got --

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:19.506
I mean -- and I should say, this
is -- these are screamers.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I think people shoul
be warned

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you've got
some real speeches

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you can throw
some spit at them.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:26.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, and I will.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will spit on you.
-Yeah, I think --

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:29.349 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:33.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please do come to my show
so I can spit on you.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:33.853 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.322
-I also want to ask, you know --
because again,

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we first met, it was when
you were on "Breaking Bad.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I always love stories
from that time.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:45.565
And you -- Aaron Paul, you know,
I know you guys are dear friends

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:47.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you worked together
for years.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.370
But you used to give him -
You used to play mind games.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:56.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, as one would to
a younger brother, you know.

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:59.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was very susceptible
and sweet.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.214 line:92%
And he was only mid-20s then

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:05.251
And I used to say to him,
"Hey, man, it's been great

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:08.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really --
it's really been great.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:11.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're going
to use this time

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go on
to really other things."

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.728 line:92%
He's like, "What do you mean?"

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:19.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "Did you read
the next script?"

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:19.732 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He goes, "No."

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "Oh, never mind,
never mind."

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:23.436 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:26.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I let it go
for a while.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.707 line:92%
And I'd say, "You know what?

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:31.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
The next best thing to being o
a show for a long time

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.146 size:84% position:42% line:92%
is a great death scene.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:33.746 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's great.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:37.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're gonna
rock that death scene, man."

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:41.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he just bought it.
He caved in.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.556 size:81% position:41% line:92%
He was like, "No, no!"

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-After everything Walter White
put him through,

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.260 size:78% position:39%
you did that as well.
-I teased him on top.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, exactly.
-He needed that as well.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:49.829 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.297 size:78% position:39%
-Hey, congratulations
on the nomination.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:51.798 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you, man.

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:53.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Both the Tony and the Tomei
-Thank you.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I hope you bring them
both home.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's Bryan Cranston,
everybody.

